36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **May**: The ferry trial closed clean, and the late-evening pilot hit its cost target. History is on our side.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"- **Benjamin**: The late-turn pool is nearly empty, and overtime is covering both final departures and overnight works.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,- **Shizue**: The ferry and rail back offices never agreed on common passenger data terms. That is a quiet wall.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: Contractor fees now outstrip our paving budget, and rates keep climbing. The money is leaking out the side door.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Benjamin, that’s a serious warning. If the pool is empty, how do we staff any new late-night routes?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @May, we can’t. The crews are a third below establishment, and the maintenance contract is the only thing with spare capacity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @May, the stopwatch shows mid-city runs are slower, but platforms clear at the old rate. The bottleneck isn’t where we think.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @May, that data wall is exactly why I checked the minutes. We cannot build a single account if the back offices refuse to speak.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, that wall explains the fees. We pay three contractors because they never agreed to share the data.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"- **May**: @Jonathan, so the pilots prove the tech works, but the politics didn’t. That’s a different problem to solve.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Midori, if the platforms clear fine, why are we hearing about crowding? Are we fixing the wrong symptom?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Benjamin, exactly. The audits say the minutes vanish in waiting for connections, not in the crush. We are chasing the noise, not the time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Benjamin, the ground hides voids, and the committees hide disagreements. We must check both before promising dates.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, precisely. The money is trapped in fees because the data never merged. We are paying for the silence.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"- **May**: So we have a staffing crisis, a data wall, and a budget leak. Which plan survives all three?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @May, none of them survive the staffing crisis. We simply do not have the hands to run anything new.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Benjamin, not if we stop adding new burdens. The data suggests we should fix the connections, not the staffing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: @Benjamin, I hear you. But if we choose nothing, the silence in the ledger grows louder.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the ledger shows the leak, not the fix. We must stop paying for the silence before we can afford the solution.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
